  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 137 PM EST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\n- Upper Low Brings Rain Wednesday then Cooler\n\nHeight falls commence this evening as shortwave upper ridging is\nreplaced by a slow moving upper low the next couple days. Still\nlooks like the bulk of the convective rains will remain south of \nthe forecast area with total QPF through Thursday generally less\nthan a quarter inch.\n\nIsolated thunderstorms are possible Wednesday afternoon but dry\nslotting occurs rather quickly as the surface low tracks across\nWisconsin and the Michigan U.P. Then cooler and showery weather\nThursday and Friday with wraparound moisture and some lake\nenhancement as mid level thermal trough axis moves through.\n\nModels have trended further north with the Sunday clipper and\nassociated precip looks to stay to the north.",
